# Bare-metal boot images, 46 MB of them. These are BUILD PRODUCTS of the
# Target-B/QEMU experiment (a Linux kernel plus an initramfs carrying thatteOS),
# not thatteOS source. The analysis document beside them IS source and is
# tracked; the images are not. Named explicitly rather than by extension
# because they have none, and a `git add -A` has swept this tree before.
baremetal/thatteos_vmlinuz
baremetal/thatteos_initramfs

# NOT PUBLISHED, deliberately, and not a build artefact — these two are SOURCE
# that stays in the working tree and out of the public repository until the PCT
# filing is secured (~Mar 2027). CLAUDE.md rule 8.
#   baremetal/ANALYSIS.txt  names THATTE@DWCNT, calls the inherited capability
#                           state a novel security primitive, and refers to the
#                           modules' patent claims.
#   CLAUDE.md               states the AC/pulse-polarity device mechanism.
# GitHub content is indexed and cached; deleting a file later does not unpublish
# it, so the decision is taken here rather than after the fact.
baremetal/ANALYSIS.txt
/CLAUDE.md
